==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*bur'a}}, akin to Bulgarian {{term|буря|lang=bg}}, Slovene {{term|burja|lang=sl}}, Serbo-Croatian {{term|бура|lang=sh}}/{{term|bura|lang=sh}}, Slovak {{term|búrka||tempest|lang=sk}} and {{term|búrať||to crush|lang=sk}}. Non-Slavic cognates include Old Norse {{term|byrr||fair wind|lang=non}}, Latin {{term|furo||I rage, rave|lang=la}}, Sanskrit {{term|भुरति||stir, palpitate|tr=bhurati|lang=sa}}. Compare also {{etyl|tr|-}} {{term|bora||squall|lang=tr}}.

